  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish that chemical SRO can be generated and varied computationally in BCC refractory HEAs using cluster-expansion/Monte Carlo or related atomistic methods, and that SRO can produce element-specific clustering or precipitates. They also document B2/BCC ordering in several HEAs and property changes caused by SRO. Thus, studying controlled SRO in another BCC refractory HEA would be plausible. However, none connects SRO in HfNbTaTiZr to HfTi/TiZr percolation pathways, reduced lattice-distortion scattering, modified high-frequency phonons, or increased lattice thermal conductivity. Reconstructing the specific transport mechanism and predicted conductivity enhancement would therefore require a substantial new idea."
